/-!
# Coordinate relation between two catalogue rows

`CoordRelation g₁ g₂ U V Φ Ψ J` packages exactly the obligations that `mission/RELEASE01_SPEC.md` §1
requires of a coordinate relation between two rows with metrics `g₁` (on the overlap `U`) and `g₂`
(on the image `V`):

* an explicit map `Φ` together with its inverse `Ψ` (`left_inv`, `right_inv`);
* `C^∞` regularity of `Φ` on `U` and of `Ψ` on `V`;
* `Φ` maps `U` bijectively onto `V` (`bijOn`);
* an explicit Jacobian `J` whose entries are proved to be genuine partial derivatives of the
  components of `Φ` (`jacobian`: `HasDerivAt` of every coordinate slice, never a junk `deriv` value);
* the pull-back identity `J(x)ᵀ · g₂(Φ x) · J(x) = g₁(x)` on `U` (`pullback`).

Like `VacuumCertificate` this is a `Prop`-valued bundle of obligations (B3 class B); each field is
discharged by a separate theorem. Ricci-flatness of the two rows is *not* part of it. Everything is
coordinate-level on `ℝ⁴`: no manifold, chart gluing or `φ ∼ φ + 2π` identification is modelled.
-/

open scoped ContDiff

namespace ExactVacuumAtlas

namespace CoordRelation

variable {g₁ g₂ : Metric 4} {U V : Set (Pt 4)} {Φ Ψ : Pt 4 → Pt 4}
  {J : Pt 4 → Matrix (Fin 4) (Fin 4) ℝ}

/-- `Ψ` maps `V` bijectively onto `U`. -/
theorem bijOn_inv (h : CoordRelation g₁ g₂ U V Φ Ψ J) : Set.BijOn Ψ V U :=
  Set.InvOn.bijOn ⟨h.right_inv, h.left_inv⟩
    (fun y hy => by
      obtain ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ := h.bijOn.surjOn hy
      rw [h.left_inv x hx]; exact hx)
    (fun x hx => h.bijOn.mapsTo hx)

end CoordRelation

end ExactVacuumAtlas

